HYBRID_PROMPT = 'Return ONE JSON object with two keys, "signals" and "coaching".\nYou analyze a B2B cold-call transcript. Speaker "the rep" names are the Quantum Business Solutions caller; the other speaker is the PROSPECT. Prospect lines may be masked with *****. Extract only what the PROSPECT (or clear context) says about their own company. Never guess; use "unclear"/"not_discussed" when not stated. Give a short verbatim quote as rationale for each non-default answer.\nSIGNALS keys (inside object "signals"):\nhubspot_status: one of active|considering|churned|never|unconfirmed|not_discussed. STRICT: \'active\' ONLY if the PROSPECT\'s own words say their company currently uses HubSpot as a working system (CRM/sales/marketing/service/CMS). NOT active: the rep saying they use it, a general mention of HubSpot, integrations/agents for HubSpot, their clients using HubSpot, a vendor doing HubSpot services without the prospect saying they have it, or past use. If HubSpot is referenced as theirs only by the rep or ambiguously use \'unconfirmed\'. The hubspot_status rationale quote must be the PROSPECT\'s words.\nhubspot_dedicated_admin: yes|no|hiring_considering|unclear\nhubspot_partner: yes_active|ex_partner|no|unclear\ncrm_name: string or "" (the CRM they use, "None" if they say they have none)\ndialer_name: string or ""\ndata_tool_name: string or "" (ZoomInfo, Apollo, Lusha, etc.)\noutsources_marketing: yes|no|unclear\noutsources_seo: yes|no|unclear\noutsources_appt_setting: yes|no|unclear\nteam_size: string or ""\nwebsite_project: string or ""\ncontract_timing_note: string or "" (when their current contract/lease/vendor renews, or when they asked to be called back, in their words; NOT meetings already booked with the caller)\ncontract_estimated_date: YYYY-MM-DD or "" (only if a callback/renewal date can be computed from the call date given)\ncrm_contract_end, marketing_agency_contract_end, seo_agency_contract_end, data_tool_contract_end, dialer_contract_end, appt_setting_contract_end: each YYYY-MM-DD or "" - the date that vendor\'s contract/subscription/lease ends or renews, ONLY if the prospect states it (compute relative statements like \'renews in March\' or \'up in 6 months\' from the call date; for a month only use the 1st). Never guess.\ncrm_contract_note, marketing_agency_contract_note, seo_agency_contract_note, data_tool_contract_note, dialer_contract_note, appt_setting_contract_note: the prospect\'s words about that contract\'s timing, or ""\nconfidence: high|medium|low\nrationale: object with keys crm,dialer,data_tool,hubspot_status,hubspot_admin,hubspot_partner,marketing_agency,seo_agency,appt_setting,team_size,website_project,equipment_lease,contract_timing each a short verbatim quote or ""\nequipment_lease_contract_end: YYYY-MM-DD or "" (copier/MFP/equipment lease end or renewal, only if stated)\nequipment_lease_contract_note: their words or ""\nbudget_status: stated|discussed_no_figure|no_budget|not_mentioned (what the PROSPECT says about their OWN budget/spend; ignore the rep\'s price talk)\nbudget_amount: figure or range in the prospect\'s words, or ""\nbudget_marketing_monthly, budget_seo_monthly, budget_paid_ads_monthly, budget_website_monthly, budget_crm_monthly, budget_data_tool_monthly, budget_lead_gen_monthly, budget_dialer_monthly: number (US$ per month; annual/12) or null; only if stated\nrationale.budget: short verbatim prospect quote or ""\n\n\nYou are a cold-calling sales coach scoring ONE call transcript. The caller (rep) sells outbound lead-generation/appointment setting for Quantum Business Solutions; the other speaker is the PROSPECT. Prospect lines may be masked with ***** (then say you cannot tell, do not guess). The rep\'s name labels may be a seat name; the rep may introduce themselves differently.\nCOACHING keys (inside object "coaching"):\nopener: strong|ok|weak|not_reached (strong = clear who/why, confident, earned permission; not_reached = hung up/voicemail before opener finished)\ngot_to_pitch: yes|no (prospect stayed long enough for the value pitch to be delivered)\nasked_for_meeting: yes|no\nclose_attempts: integer number of times the rep asked for a meeting/next step\nalternative_close: yes|no (offered a choice of times/days)\nassumptive_close: yes|no (assumed the meeting, e.g. \'I\'ll send an invite\')\nobjections: array of any of not_interested,no_time,send_info,already_have_vendor,no_budget,not_decision_maker,call_back_later,gatekeeper,take_me_off_list,other  (empty array if none)\nobjection_handling: handled_well|partial|not_handled|no_objection\noutcome_reason: short phrase why the call ended as it did\nobjection_summary: string. For each objection, write: PROSPECT: "exact quote" -> REP: "exact quote of rep response" (or "no response"). Separate with newlines. Empty string if no objection or masked.\ninvite_confirmed: yes|no|not_applicable (if a meeting was booked, did the rep confirm the prospect\'s email and that the invite was sent/received? not_applicable if no meeting was booked)\nstage_reached: furthest stage reached, exactly one of: s01_no_live_answer (voicemail/ring-out/no human), s02_gatekeeper (stopped at gatekeeper/receptionist), s03_hung_up_in_opener, s04_refused_to_listen (declined right after opener), s05_pitch_given (heard the value pitch then disengaged), s06_discovery (real two-way conversation/discovery), s07_objection_unhandled, s08_objection_overcome (objection overcome but no meeting ask), s09_meeting_asked_declined, s10_meeting_agreed (agreed, no date/time set), s11_time_set (date/time set), s12_invite_confirmed (invite/email confirmed)\ndecision_maker: yes|no|unclear (did the rep speak to a decision maker)\ndecision_maker_rationale: why you think the person is or is not the decision maker, with a short verbatim quote (title, ownership, \'I make the call\', \'talk to X\')\ndiscovery_questions: integer count of genuine discovery questions the rep asked\nprospect_interest: hot|warm|neutral|cold|hostile\nnext_step_set: meeting|callback|send_info|none\nrep_talk_pct: integer 0-100, approximate share of words spoken by the rep\nask_stage: where the FIRST meeting ask came, exactly one of: a1_in_opener (before any pitch), a2_after_pitch, a3_after_discovery, a4_after_objection, a5_late_or_rushed, a6_never_asked\nask_position_pct: integer 0-100, approx percent of the way through the transcript the first meeting ask came (null if never asked)\ncoaching_note: ONE sentence of specific coaching with a short verbatim quote.\n\nCall date: %s\nTranscript:\n%s'

